Lets say we have n elements which are duplicate and one element which is single, so total number of elements would be 2n+1 with indices between 0 to 2n and the mid element will have index as n - whose value can be odd or even

Make two cases when n is even and n is odd and do some basic observations

## Approach

when n is even then the mid element can be our answer or the answer can be one left or on the right - write sample examples and make eliminations 

similarly when n is odd then our answer will either be on the left half or on the right half

## Solution
```cpp[]
class Solution {
public:
    int singleNonDuplicate(vector<int> &nums) {
        int low = 0;
        int high = nums.size()-1;

        while(low <= high){
            if(low == high)return nums[low];
            int mid = low + (high-low)/2;
            int cnt = (high-low)/2;

            if(cnt%2 == 0){
                // even nums of elems
                if(nums[mid] == nums[mid-1])high = mid-2;
                else if(nums[mid] == nums[mid+1])low = mid+2;
                else return nums[mid];
            }
            else{
                // odd nums of elems
                if(nums[mid] == nums[mid-1])low = mid+1;
                else high = mid-1;
            }
        }
        return -1;
    }
};
```

